<design_philosophy>
NoteSecret follows a "Calm Technology" philosophy — the app serves the user without demanding attention. The UX is built on three pillars:

1. **Zero Friction**: No login, no onboarding walls, no mandatory permissions. Open the app → start writing. The fastest path from thought to note.

2. **Thumb-Zone Architecture**: All primary actions (create note, search, navigate) are placed within the natural thumb reach zone (bottom 60% of screen). Navigation bar is anchored at the bottom. The FAB (Floating Action Button) for "New Note" sits at the bottom-right corner — the most accessible touch point for right-handed users (with left-hand mode option in settings).

3. **Content-First Hierarchy**: UI chrome is minimal. The note content is the hero. Toolbars, labels, and metadata fade into the background. When the user is writing, the editor goes into a distraction-free mode with only essential formatting controls visible.

Typography uses serif fonts (Lora & Merriweather) to evoke the feeling of printed books and handwritten journals — a deliberate contrast to the sans-serif dominated app landscape. This gives NoteSecret a distinctive, timeless identity.

Whitespace is treated as a design element, not wasted space. Generous padding, breathing room between cards, and soft earthy tones create a sense of calm and order.
</design_philosophy>

