<gestures_and_haptics>
The app is snappy, instant, and silent — like a precision tool:

- Tap: Immediate response. Button scales down to 0.97 with 100ms opacity fade (0.7 → 1.0). No haptic vibration.
- Long Press: Activates multi-select mode on notes list, or shows context menu (pin, lock, color, delete).
- Swipe Right: Quick action — Pin/Unpin note (on notes list).
- Swipe Left: Quick action — Delete note (with undo snackbar).
- Pull to Refresh: Not needed (offline-first, no sync). Disabled to avoid confusion.
- Scroll: Standard Flutter scroll physics. Fast deceleration. No bounce on Android (ClampingScrollPhysics).
- Back Navigation: System back gesture or top-left back arrow. Predictive back gesture support on Android 14+.
- Transitions: Instant push/pop with minimal 150ms fade. No spring physics, no parallax, no page curl. Sheets and modals slide from bottom with 200ms duration.
- Haptics: NONE. Zero vibration. The app is completely silent. Visual feedback only.
- Keyboard: Editor auto-focuses with soft keyboard. Formatting toolbar sits above keyboard (InputAccessoryView pattern).
</gestures_and_haptics>

