<data_strategy>
<storage>
Full Local — Isar NoSQL Database.
All data stored on-device in app's private directory.
No cloud sync. No remote server. No analytics. No telemetry.
Database schema:
- Notes: id, title, body (rich text/markdown), color, isPinned, isLocked, folderId, tags[], attachments[], createdAt, updatedAt, deletedAt (soft delete).
- Folders: id, name, emoji, sortOrder, createdAt.
- Tags: id, name, color, createdAt.
- Settings: key-value pairs stored in SharedPreferences.
- Backup format: JSON export of all tables → AES-256 encrypted → .notesecret file extension.
</storage>

<auth_security>
- No user account / login. Zero authentication barrier.
- App-level: Optional PIN (4-6 digits) stored in flutter_secure_storage (Keystore on Android).
- Biometric: Optional fingerprint/face via local_auth. Used for Vault access and locked notes.
- Per-note lock: Individual notes can be flagged as locked. Requires biometric/PIN to view content.
- Backup encryption: AES-256-CBC with user-defined password. Password is NOT stored — user must remember it.
- Auto-lock: Vault auto-locks when app moves to background. Configurable timeout.
- No data leaves the device unless user explicitly exports or creates a backup.
</auth_security>
</data_strategy>

